==Strategy==
Welcome to Realm of Carnage 2.0. The Razorbacks and M. Ost may make this stage sound like one hell of a fight, but there is one difference that makes this stage a lot easier: besides the Sir Seal, nothing in this stage is infinite. Once the Ginger Snaches, M. Ost and Razorbacks are defeated, they're gone for good. Razorback and the Ginger Snaches are the least of your concerns here, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and other [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark units]] will get rid of him with ease, while [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] will juggle the Ginger Snaches. M. Ost also shouldn't cause that much trouble, just use your [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relics]] like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] and [[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Bargain Cat]] to beat M. Ost to a pulp. It's also possible to lure M. Ost and rush it down with [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]]. Once M. Ost is defeated, Hannya on her own poses virtually no threat. Use speedy [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]] (e.g. the aforementioned Courier Cat + [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]]) to defeat her and win.

==Trivia==
*Kernel Chaos's Japanese name, Konton Kōn Zōn (混沌コーンゾーン, "Chaos Corn Zone", may play off of how 混沌 (chaos) and 渾沌 (steamed [[wikipedia:Manjū|manjū]] or steamed mochi) are both read as ''konton''.

